From 0f8f39257a3733ed6f707e7bb77ad1113e766471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tron <tron@tsmconsultz.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 02:43:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(finops): gate unconditional auto-escalation timer
 behind tsm_auto_mode

tsmAutoRunFinOps() fired 600ms after page load with no tsm_auto_mode
check and hard-navigated to finops-executive-portal.html exactly 3200ms
later, unconditionally. Every other vertical's equivalent auto-run hook
(legal's fireEngines, etc.) checks tsm_auto_mode !== 'off' before
scheduling itself. This one didn't, meaning any real visitor on the
FinOps Strategist page got silently redirected to the Exec Portal
~3.2s after load, and Playwright demo recordings always ended up on
the wrong page for relay-banner and push-to-exec steps regardless of
Groq response speed.

Fix: wrap the auto-fire setTimeout in the same tsm_auto_mode check
every other vertical already uses, matching the codebase's established
pattern.
---
 html/finops-suite/finops-war/finops-main-strategist.html | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/html/finops-suite/finops-war/finops-main-strategist.html b/html/finops-suite/finops-war/finops-main-strategist.html
index 1b17901a..6804bee4 100644
--- a/html/finops-suite/finops-war/finops-main-strategist.html
+++ b/html/finops-suite/finops-war/finops-main-strategist.html
@@ -1754,7 +1754,9 @@ function tsmAutoRunFinOps() {
 }
 
 // AUTO FIRE HOOK
-setTimeout(tsmAutoRunFinOps, 600);
+if (localStorage.getItem('tsm_auto_mode') !== 'off') {
+  setTimeout(tsmAutoRunFinOps, 600);
+}
 </script><script>
 // ===== TSM_AUTONOMY_STANDARDIZED =====
 window.TSM_AUTONOMY_STANDARDIZED = true;
-- 
